     "text": "GROUNDING: grounded\nMISSING INPUTS: none\n\nCOMPETITOR 1\nProduct: Ada\nVendor: Ada Inc.\nPricing: Ada's pricing is primarily custom, tailored for each client's specifications; no exact figures are publicly available .\nAccuracy: Vendor states high accuracy with machine learning and advanced natural language processing .\nLatency: Vendor highlights fast response times designed for high-volume environments .\nComparison: Ada supports voice and knowledge base but lacks transparent pricing to compare costs directly.\n\nCOMPETITOR 2\nProduct: Netomi AI\nVendor: Netomi\nPricing: Netomi offers custom pricing models based on customer needs; specific costs are not publicly detailed on their site .\nAccuracy: Vendor states an accuracy rate of 85% for its chatbot solutions .\nLatency: No source found.\nComparison: Netomi emphasizes high accuracy and robust knowledge base integration but does not appear to prioritize voice capabilities.\n\nCOMPETITOR 3\nProduct: Kore.ai\nVendor: Kore.ai Inc.\nPricing: Pricing ranges from $50 to $180 per month for self-serve plans, with usage-based billing for other tiers starting at $0.20/session\u301010:1\u2020source\u3011.\nAccuracy: Vendor states their platform is built for high accuracy, leveraging natural language processing and generative AI capabilities\u301010:1\u2020source\u3011.\nLatency: Voice sessions are billed per 15-minute interaction, but no specific latency figures are provided\u301010:0\u2020source\u3011.\nComparison: Kore.ai features robust voice and knowledge base support that aligns well with the described feature, but the pay-as-you-go billing model can lead to unpredictable costs.",
